## Error Handling in Controllers

Map DomainError types to HTTP status codes.

```java
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;

import java.util.Map;

class OrderController {

    private ResponseEntity<?> handleError(Exception error) {

        if (error instanceof DomainError domainError) {
            int status = switch (domainError.getType()) {
                case NOT_FOUND -> 404;
                case VALIDATION -> 422;
                default -> 400;
            };

            return ResponseEntity
                    .status(status)
                    .body(Map.of("error", domainError.getMessage()));
        }

        // Technical error - log and return 500
        error.printStackTrace();

        return ResponseEntity
                .status(500)
                .body(Map.of("error", "Internal server error"));
    }
}
```

